    "text": "Let n be a positive integer, and let G ⩽ GL(n, Z) be finitely generated. Given\na bound b ∈ N, let eb be the number of elements of G all of whose matrix entries have\nabsolute value ⩽ b. Does the limit lim ln eb / ln b always exist?              S. Kohl\n                                      b→∞",
